  "scientific_conclusions": [
    "In one archived visitor environment, the original Model3 conditional expected high-allele direction of matching switches from negative in early years to positive in late years; initial negative selfed-seed directional contribution becomes positive while father/mother outcross terms remain negative.",
    "All-three-factor equalization on the SAME source parent population shifts expected matching high-allele direction up, investment high-allele direction down, and assurance high-allele direction up, in both budget regimes.",
    "In standard budget8 at year8, matching and assurance effects of this specific outcross-only counterfactual mostly reflect maternal recipient allele-weighted marginal changes; investment male and female changes are similar in size.",
    "These are exact algebraic contributions within source reproductive pair-weight model and do not identify selfing, pollinator behavior or maternal fecundity as independent causal ecological mechanisms.",
    "The matching-direction sign reversal can arise from genotype state evolution, changes in the archived visitor sequence, and their interaction. This experiment has not isolated those competing explanations.",
    "No natural plants, independent islands, confirmatory visitor history seeds or validated SDE/SPDE."
  ]
